{%- comment -%}
PFC Pulse Trend — the Daily Pulse over 30 days: per-lever days-on-target
(worst first), how many days were primed for a great day, and the standing fix
for the chronic miss. pfc-pulse answers tonight; this answers lately.

Every count on this screen is GOOD days out of the window — high is always
good, on every number, in every view. Never print an off-count next to an
on-count (AGENTS.md § "Metrics point one direction").

Each lever carries its 30-day verdict spelled out — GREEN / YELLOW / RED, not
punctuation marks. Those need a legend, and a legend that isn't on the screen
is a legend nobody has. Same vocabulary on every screen — STATUS_WORD in
trmnl_push.py.

The Goal column shows the bare threshold. Never render last night's
distance-to-next-tier here — on a 30-day window it reads as a property of the
window and isn't one (the builder uses `target_plain`).

Data comes pre-digested from pulse.py (pulse_history, pulse_levers,
chronic_misses) via build_pfc_pulse_trend; templates only print. Counts instead of
status glyphs by design — a handful of ranked rows are legible across a room, a
grid of hundreds of status marks is not. No emoji; targets arrive
transliterated (>=, <=) because the comparison glyphs fail on e-ink too.
{%- endcomment -%}
